## Introduction

R Markdown puts writing, code, and results in one report. I used mtcars to look at gas mileage.

## Math

Here is math in a sentence: $\alpha + \beta = \gamma$.

Here is the formula for an average:

$$
\bar{x} = \frac{\sum x_i}{n}
$$

## Load Data

```{r}
data(mtcars)
head(mtcars)
```

## Gas Mileage

This code shows a summary of gas mileage.

```{r}
summary(mtcars$mpg)
```

## Plot

```{r}
plot(mtcars$wt, mtcars$mpg)
```

Heavier cars generally get lower gas mileage.

## Reflection

I like having the writing and code together. It saves me from copying results into a separate report.

